  "notes": "A compound of {保|ほ} (preserve) and {湿|しつ} (moisture). Almost always used in skincare and beauty contexts to refer to keeping skin hydrated.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {保湿|ほしつ}クリーム: moisturizing cream\n- {保湿|ほしつ}{成分|せいぶん}: moisturizing ingredients\n- {保湿|ほしつ}ケア: moisturizing care/routine\n- {保湿|ほしつ}{力|りょく}: moisturizing power\n- {保湿|ほしつ}{効果|こうか}: moisturizing effect\n- {保湿|ほしつ}する: to moisturize (suru verb)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {乾燥|かんそう}: dryness, drying out — the opposite condition\n- {潤|うるお}い: moisture, hydration — the desired result\n\nUSAGE:\nParticularly relevant in {冬|ふゆ} (winter) when {乾燥|かんそう} (dryness) is a common concern. Skincare routines in Japan typically emphasize {保湿|ほしつ} as a key step after {洗顔|せんがん} (face washing).",
